NetNewsWire instrumentation patch for the MSc benchmark.
Origin: original, 
Upstream: https://github.com/Ranchero-Software/NetNewsWire @ bb5ab3dc91f9da00fa8eaedf89a04c5e7970ad5c (main)

Apply (from the repo root):
  git clone https://github.com/Ranchero-Software/NetNewsWire apps/external/netnewswire
  git -C apps/external/netnewswire checkout bb5ab3dc91f9da00fa8eaedf89a04c5e7970ad5c
  (cd apps/external/netnewswire && printf '\n\nuk.ac.city.parag\n' | ./setup.sh)   # empty Team ID, no signing
  cp apps/external/netnewswire-Instrumentation.swift apps/external/netnewswire/iOS/Instrumentation.swift
  git -C apps/external/netnewswire apply ../netnewswire.patch
Build (run twice from clean: the first build can race with SecretKey.swift generation):
  xcodebuild -project NetNewsWire.xcodeproj -scheme NetNewsWire-iOS -configuration Debug \
    -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 17,OS=27.0' -derivedDataPath build \
    -skipMacroValidation -skipPackagePluginValidation CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO build
Bundle id: uk.ac.city.parag.NetNewsWire.iOS-DEBUG (from the org identifier given to setup.sh).
iOS/ is a synchronised folder, so Instrumentation.swift joins the app target without a project edit.

Contents:
  Instrumentation only, no build fixes needed (D-019; spec docs/external-perturbations.md):
  Instrumentation.swift: Perturb enum (8 flags nn01..nn08), UnlabelledSymbol bitmap, ResetData, ResearchUI hooks.
  AppDelegate.swift: ResetData.wipeIfRequested() first in didFinishLaunching; ResetData.seedIfRequested()
    after the first-run block; the default (network) feed import is skipped when -resetData is given.
  MainFeedCollectionViewController.swift: toolbar ids addButton/settingsButton and nn01/nn02/nn07/nn08;
    nn04 subtitles on the Add action sheet (tap) and the long-press UIMenu; nn05 label override per cell.
  MainFeedCollectionViewCell.swift: accessibilityLabelOverride honoured by the accessibilityLabel getter.
  SettingsViewController.swift: nn03 subtitle rows and nn06 generic switch labels.

